AUTHOR BIOGRAPHIES
Mara Blake serves as the head of the Data and Visualization Services department in the Libraries at NC State University. The department pro
vides expert assistance and specialized spaces to help affiliates learn how to find, use, analyse and visualize data and has operated a Data Sci
ence Consulting program since 2018. The Data Science Consulting program leverages a mix of professional staff and graduate students to
serve the needs of the NC State Community and collaborates closely with the Consulting Program in the Data Science Academy led by Emily
Griffith. More information can be found on the webpage https://www.lib.ncsu.edu/staff/department/data-visualization-services for Data and
Visualization Services. Blake was a co-investigator on the Alfred P. Sloan Foundation grant that supported this work.
Emily Griffith is an associate professor of the practice in the Department of Statistics and the Director of Data Science Consulting in the NC
State Data Science Academy (DSA). Griffith was a co-investigator on the Alfred P. Sloan Foundation grant that supported this work. The
DSA's Collaborative Consulting Corps is fully integrated with the Libraries programming led by Mara Blake, working with graduate students to
provide project-based data science support to researchers across campus. More information can be found on the webpage https://
datascienceacademy.ncsu.edu/data-science-consulting/ for the DSA's Collaborative Consulting Corps.
Steven J. Pierce is associate director at Michigan State University's Center for Statistical Training and Consulting. Among other duties, he
coordinates the consulting operations by assigning cases to consultants. Expertise in applied statistics, program evaluation, data management,
